Hi Glen,

[I copied FSG OP Architecture on this reply, because
many people want to know about XML Schema tools.]

I _edit_ XML Schema with a plaintext editor (my own).

I _graphically_view_ XML Schema with XML Spy ($399 
for standard edition, from Altova in Germany), which 
the IEEE/ISTO PWG just graciously bought me a copy of.  
Download a free 30-day evaluation copy from:

	http://www.altova.com/

I _textually_view_ XML Schema with the quite wonderful
(free) tool XRay from Architag.  Highly recommended
for colorized plaintext viewing.  This would probably
also be an excellent editor.  Download the free tool 
from:

	http://www.architag.com/xray/

I _validate_ XML Schema with three tools:  XML Spy,
XRay, and the excellent (free) XML Schema Validator
(co-written by one of the W3C authors of the XML
standards).  Find current status and a download link
for the self-installing Win32 version of XSV at:

	http://www.ltg.ed.ac.uk/~ht/xsv-status.html

Cheers,
